{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/690569-your-ascended-scions","id":690569,"title":"Your Ascended Scions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-05T16:29:29-07:00","id":690569,"title":"Your Ascended Scions?","content":"So I've had this idea for a while and it won't stop bugging me until I get it out of my system. Anyways, the purpose of this thread is to post ideas / examples of Scions you've had that managed to obtain godhood. I had originally planned to upload 4 characters, but felt that would take up too much space and the ones I have now have gone through several rewrites and imaginings, so I'm having trouble coming up with the other two. So to start off, I'll just post the first two until I complete the others.<br /> <br /> <br /> First, let me clarify that I am terrible when it comes to thinking up names, especially foreign language names. I have no idea what would be appropriate for the majority of the pantheons, so I either chose an English name for them, or I used a translator and picked a word or phrase that suited their personality.<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nariko:</b> Goddess of Silence and former scion of Raiden. If her father is the god of lightning, Nariko is the calm before the storm, that first droplet of rain that heralds the beginning of a flood. Nariko follows the path of the shinobi, otherwise known as the ninja. But she is not the black clad, sword swinging assassin that mortals have misenterpreted her kind to be. She embraces the way of nonexistence, channeling the void into herself. In this war against the Titans, Nariko moves unseen and unheard, yet her handiwork is present all the same. She is willing to utilize any means at her disposal to achieve victory over the enemy, regardless if such tactics would sacrifice her honor and pride. As such, she has proven to have the nature of a Rogue, caring little for the rules of fair combat and more on the results of such battles.<br /> <br /> Since her rise to divinity, Nariko has become the patron lady of assassins, saboteurs, the dishonored, the deaf and the mute. Many of her worshipers swear vows of silence to honor their goddess. Her priests communicate with each other almost entirely through whispering. There are no spoken prayers to Nariko, instead her worshipers silently offer their gratitude and requests to her in a state of meditative reverie. Her temples are custom made to either muffle or enhance sounds that occur within it, as a way to either aid their commitment or locate disruptions.<br /> <br /> In her godly form, Nariko never utters a sound, refusing to speak and instead conveying her thoughts in the form of writing or body language. She also covers her entire body from head to toe, leaving her true appearance a mystery to all. Her clothing is the pale blue garb of the traditional ninja, with her face being covered in a featureless mask, save for a pair of slits near the eye sockets allowing her to see. Some legends claim that Nariko has become one with the void itself and that her godly form is actually a set of empty garments wrapped around her divine essence. Regardless if this is true, nobody has yet had the opportunity to strip her down and find out. Few would dare to attempt it anyways, lest they suffer her vengeance.<br /> <br /> In her mortal disguises, Nariko is more prone to social interaction, though remains soft spoken and aloof none the less. She often takes the role of somebody who works behind the scenes, having a part in the action without being openly involved. She has been a financial backer, a consultant, a third party contractor, a private security director and a hitwoman. It is in mortal disguise that Nariko performs most of her visitations, for it is the only time she chooses to actually relay verbal messages.<br /> <br /> Scions of Nariko have a tendency to be introvertive, keeping their emotions suppressed behind a face of disenterest and monotone voice. They do not speak much because they usually don't know what to say or have nothing to add to the conversation. If they had been ordinary mortals, their behavior might render them outcasts by the rest of society for being weird and unfriendly. But as children of the gods, it makes them come across as being men and women of action, preferring to let their deeds speak for them instead of making proud boasts and empty threats!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Associated Powers:</b> Epic Dexterity, Epic Manipulation, Tsukumo-Gami, Darkness, Illusion, Mystery, Psychopomp<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities:</b> Thrown, Athletics, Medicine, Awareness, Marksmanship, Stealth, Melee<br /> <br /> <b>Rivals:</b> Amaterasu, Vidar, Hachiman, Athena<br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>David:</b> God of Audacity and former Scion of Set. Born and raised in America, David knew virtually nothing about the Pesedjet's religious doctrines until after Set visited him. Facing thousands of years worth of culture shock, David earned himself a reputation as a Rebel, constantly acting in defiance of the Pesedjet in favor of his own moral standing and beliefs. His rise to godhood has fed his ego to obnoxious growth. He is loud, proud and cares little for rules and expectations if they conflict with his personal beliefs. He is a potential threat to the strict order the Pesedjet adhere to, which is exactly how Set wants him!<br /> <br /> Since his ascension to godhood, David has become the patron lord of the weak, the crippled, the under privilaged and the boastful. His blind arrogance is both his greatest weakness and his greatest strength. Many times has David overestimated his abilities in this war and landed himself in trouble. However, there are also many times when David has stood his ground, comitting himself whole heartedly to a cause he believes in and facing down the enemy with a fearless expression on his face. Such boldness has inspired the mortals to view him as a role model in the face of adversity and doubt. His fellow Pesedjet, however, view his careless disregard for the rules to be dangerous and unpredictable.<br /> <br /> David enjoys skirting expectations so much that he even began to study the purview of ice and snow just to prove that he could! Disregarding the fact that the Pesedjet is a religion originating from the desert and that such an element is something they would be totally unaccustomed to. Immediately following his ascension, David celebrated his new status by making it snow for seven hours in the Sahara Desert, a 'miracle' which reaffirmed his cult's belief in his divine heritage.<br /> <br /> In his true form, David is the badger headed god, an animal which he adopted as a practical joke but soon became a religious symbol associated with him. His skin is much lighter than most of the Pesedjet, yet still retains a hint of tan from his family ancestry. His clothing is minimalist, consisting of the iconic, white kilt and excessive jewelry associated with males of the pantheon. His personal gemstones are the topaz and the amythest, fastened into his jewelery in a repeated sequence. His body is in great physical condition and nearly flawless in appearance, which further inspires his vanity and pride.<br /> <br /> When in the mortal world, David likes to remain unpredictable. Just when you think you know what kind of disguise he'll take, he likes to pull the bait and switch, choosing a form or lifestyle nobody could have guessed. Regardless of what form he chooses, however, his strong will in the face of oppression remains. David has been a grand architect, a controversial celebrity, a rebel group leader and there was even a time he disguised himself as new convert to his own cult!<br /> <br /> Scions of David are a wild and passionate bunch who's actions are viewed with both admiration and unease depending on who's watching them. They act and speak with such determination that it is easy to be swept up in their charisma and follow them. However, it is also easy for them to suffer from over inflated egoes and lead such admirers to ruin if they aren't careful. David's Scions are excelent motivators who certainly know how to give a rallying speech in battle, you just don't want them to be placed in charge of your main force. Because chances are they'll be the 'no quarter' type of general who fights to the last man.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Associated Powers:</b> Epic Charisma, Epic Strength, Animal (Badger), Heku, Chaos, Frost, War, Earth<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities:</b> Larceny, Control, Craft, Integrity, Brawl, Presence<br /> <br /> <b>Rivals:</b> Horus, Tyr, Autum-Re, Ogoun, Tezcatlipoca","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-05-2015, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T18:27:47-07:00","id":690685,"title":"","content":"We never got that far, but a group of mine did plan our scions ascension and eventual divine titles/mantles.<br /> <br /> We had a scion whose patron was Ryujin and would have eventually become the God of Shinobi and Serpents. His true blood was Yamata no Orochi.<br /> <br /> Another was Jenjin a Scion of Tsuki-yomi. He was a budding mangaka He would have become the patron of Archers and Artists.<br /> <br /> There was also Enishi Yamada. He was a scion of Mikaboshi. He worked for his father at first, but defected. With his deeds and backing from from Tsuki-yomi and Susano-o he would have eventually been accepted into the Amatsu-kami. He would have be the God of Night (a sort of God of the comforting darkness) with a dual aspect of being <i>the</i> Shini-gami.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T08:31:34-07:00","id":691285,"title":"","content":"In the game we ran (it took 3 GMs working in tandem), we got several characters to godhood, but only a few were actually God of Something (i.e. had maxed out a purview), since it\u2019s been years I can\u2019t remember all the associated powers...and this is not a complete list, there's gonna be more.<br /> <br /> <u>Askrir, Arranger of the Gods; Former Scion of Loki.</u><br /> Distinguished himself throughout his scion career by brokering favors between scions, lesser immortals, and other quasi-allied creatures. His connections allowed him to position himself to; Convince Fenrir not to take part in the battle of Ragnarok, by finding him a place he could roam free. Convince Jormungandr (at another god\u2019s urging) to Invade the Drowned Road along with the forgotten titan Okeanos and take over the power structure, replacing him with Ahzi-Dahaka the minion of Ahriman. Trick that strange titan avatar Tuisco into filling in for Tyr, and thus take over Tyr\u2019s doom, all so that Tyr could arbitrate the duel between Loki and Heimdall, forcing Loki to fight fair (and thus fail to kill Heimdall).<br /> <br /> <u>Cait Llyd, King of the Tuatha; Former Scion of Lugh.</u><br /> Started a literal musical band of scions and audaciously used his music career to gather a huge following, seeding his actual adventures in as part of his epic rock ballads. Ascended to the throne after leading the battle to retake Mag Mell as a demigod, and then leading numerous successful campaigns against the Titans menacing other pantheons. Also carried the most geasa ever known to be in effect on a single person without them self-destructing.<br /> <br /> <u>Athanasia, Goddess of Intrigue and Diplomacy; former Scion of Hera</u><br /> Formed a cult of personailty to herself culminating in an actual cult at demigodhood in order to accumulate influence throughout the modern world. Embarked on diplomatic missions to various magical beings in order to build up allies for the gods. Worked out a deal to secure the loyalty of the displaced titans of light (led by Hyperion) by assisting with the dethroning of Aten. Embarked upon a quest to restore Niflheim the titanrealm of frost to active status (in order to balance Muspelheim), and earned the loyalty of Utgard-loki (its new dominant avatar) and all of the Jotnar. Successfully pled the case of the next generation gods at the courts of Anu, winning the divine right of rule from the overtitan of Justice/Order.<br /> <br /> <u>Iukine-Rahiti, God of Excessive Force and Destruction; Former Scion of Pele</u><br /> Destroyed: facility devoted to producing corrupt titan-scions, a cult dedicated to unleashing aspects of Vritra into the world, in incursion of drowned road beings (deep ones essentially) into Chicago by luring them all into a club and detonating it (and the city block), Several battalions of Firbolg at Mag Mell, a section of Kronus\u2019s forces invading Mt. Olympus (singlehandedly), an army of rakshasa attacking Mt. Meru (along with some other gods).<br /> <br /> <u>Damali-Anshah, God of Dreams; Former Scion of Vayu</u><br /> Set up a network of informants and brokers to support all scions in the war all over the world. Established a network of temple/museums that were mystically charged to act as touchstones all around the world while preserving the ancient cultures of ALL the pantheons. Collected all the dead mortal souls who were not corrupted into specters or converted to the worship of the gods into a permanent dreamworld where they were allowed to live on. Created a complex geomantic working to funnel the power of legend up to the overworld to assist all of the gods (and fuel his own projects). Conceived of the plan to substitute Ahzi-Dahaka for Jormungandr at Ragnarok (using Askrir) in order to twist fate to the gods favor, and arranged for the return of Cerebus and Orthrus to Hades in order to secure his Underworld and free up his forces.<br /> <br /> <u>Andariel, Ascended titanspawn of Night; Scion of Nyx (neutral titaness )</u><br /> Acted as a spy/double agent unknowingly, used by Nyx to unravel the plots of rival titans along with whatever hapless scions he happened to be with, then eventually gave himself over willingly once he learned her ultimate plan was just to free her husband Erebus from bondage and restore him to prominence. Loaned out to the gods on occasion for their \u201cassistance\u201d with this plan, mostly at his request, eventually acted as a liaison to the gods for the titans of Night.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":765,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","user":"Darksol-aeternium","date":"02-08-2016, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T09:57:37-07:00","id":692643,"title":"","content":"<b>Jaina &amp; Ranko:</b> Twin Deities of Rain and former Scions of Poseidon. Two Scions conceived by the same god on the same day in the same womb, Jaina and Ranko share an unusual fate. Only capable of accessing their full power when in proximity to each other, they are essentially one god with two bodies. When seperated from each other, their power is only at half strength, with their abilities and purviews divided between them. But when they get close, they can draw on the other's abilities to compliment their own. Jaina and Ranko also share a form of twin telepathy, experiencing each others pain both emotional and physical. It is believed that if one were to die, they would both perish.<br /> <br /> As deities, Jaina is a compassionate and gentle goddess of rain and harvest. Ranko, however, is a wrathful and and savage god of monsoons and floods. When dealing with others, it is typically Jaina who takes the lead in matters of social grace and etiquette. But when it's time to lay down divine retribution, Ranko takes charge with a mighty storm! They are possessed of a dual nature, with Jaina as a Caregiver and Ranko as a Cynic.<br /> <br /> Since their ascension to godhood, Jaina and Ranko have always been depicted as a pair. Their temples never have shrines or statues devoted to one or the other, but worship both in unison. Their cultists pray to Jaina to bring them bountiful harvests and fair weather, while fearing her brother's vengeance should they offend her. Offerings are made in the form of a share of the crops grown from Jaina's life giving rains, placating the twins with a home grown feast!<br /> <br /> In their godly forms, Jaina and Ranko are nearly identical twins with the exception of obvious gender palettes. They appear as young adults, possibly in their mid 20's. Their hair is dark black and grown to the shoulders in length. Their eyes are dark green and they wear garments fashioned out of the bones and scales of various species of fish. As befits her gentle disposition, Jaina's body is fair to look upon and soft to the touch, while her more violent brother is ruggedly handsome with firm muscle tone.<br /> <br /> When in the mortal world, Jaina and Ranko are nearly inseperable, mostly because they're afraid of being caught off guard by random Titan attacks. Their disguises tend to resemble family businesses or close knit partnerships. The sister acting as the public face of the company while her brother deals with security and legal actions to keep things running smoothly. Despite their closeness, they usually conceive Scions individually unless they're in a particularly kinky mood and feel like sharing their lovers.<br /> <br /> Regardless of which twin the Scion is descended from, they have the capacity to inherit either of their abilities and often inherit a mixture of both. This further leads credence to the idea that Jaina and Ranko are spiritually one deity, instead of consolidating power between two. It is also common for them to share dual personalities, taking on an almost completely altered disposition according to their mood at the time. They can be welcoming and friendly when in a good mood, or violent and destructive when provoked. All in all, the children of these two gods are people who's good side it is best to stay on.<br /> <br /> <b>Associated Powers: </b><br /> <br /> Jaina - Epic Charisma, Water, Arete, Fertility, Animal (Horse)<br /> <br /> Ranko - Epic Strength, Sky, Arete, War, Animal (Bull)<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities:</b><br /> <br /> Jaina - Presence, Animal Ken, Empathy<br /> <br /> Ranko - Thrown, Melee, Athletics<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-11-2015, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T22:44:54-08:00","id":760511,"title":"","content":"<b>Name:</b> Kujaku no Oji<br /> <br /> <b>Nature:</b> Perfectionist<br /> <br /> <b>Info: </b>God of Beauty and a former Scion of Hachiman. Abandoning his mortal name upon his ascension to godhood, it is believed that only those who personally knew him before such an event remember who he used to be. He is now known to the world as Kujaku no Oji, otherwise known as Prince of Peacocks. In Kujaku's mind, he is a flawless expression of beauty and grace, taking great joy in flaunting his perfection in front of others. Almost everything not following the Amatsukami's religious culture is hideous and deserving of mockery so far as he's concerned. He also feels that warriors who rely on brute strength or endless stamina are unrefined oafs who have neither poise nor elegance and he is fond of taunting them on the subject unless he believes they can defeat him in battle.<br /> <br /> In appearance, Kujaku no Oji comes across as being sexually androgynous to most who look upon him. He possesses a boyish physique, but is graced with effeminate beauty and charm. His eyes are bright green while his dark hair remains shiny and smooth nearly all the time. His manner of dress is often flashy and over stylized, exhibiting bright colors and eye catching patterns. More often than not, such attire looks like it was designed for the opposite sex, yet Kujaku flaunts it around like it was custom ordered! His speech is perfectly articulated with a dignified tone and a high laugh that is a few notes higher pitched than it should be.<br /> <br /> Being a child of Hachiman, Kujaku no Oji is no stranger to combat and uses a two handed battle fan that has been painted like a peacock's tail. But when he engages the field, he does so with lethal precision. While his opponent is busy pounding their chest and making grand boasts of their power in battle, Kujaku is already planning which vital areas to target first. A duel with Kujaku is often ended so quickly that his opponent doesn't even realize what happened until it's too late. When facing multiple foes at once, Kujaku's movements resemble dancing as he weaves in an out of range, striking his opponents in the most effecient manner before moving onto the next. <br /> <br /> Being as vainglorious as Kujaku is, he demands that his Scions exhibit the same level of elegance as himself. If he perceives his child to be ugly or ill mannered, he will disavow his affiliation with them, letting them continue believing they are ordinary mortals unless another god chooses to adopt them. The ones that he does claim undergo strict mentorship in an effort to guide them as close to perfection as is possible. This process has a tendency to leave his Scions overconfident in their abilities, but they perform so well that this arrogance isn't completely unjustified.<br /> <br /> <b>Associated Powers:</b> Epic Charisma, Epic Dexterity, Epic Wits, Tsukumo-Gami, Animal (Peacock), Health, Sun, Star<br /> <br /> <b>Assosciated Abilities:</b> Presence, Athletics, Melee, Command, Art, Integrity","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T20:15:52-08:00","id":768908,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <b>Deleted, due to silliness</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-11-2015, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T12:11:16-08:00","id":769452,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Lypeos/Theraos</b></u><br /> <b>Role: </b>God of Social Events and Misfortune/God of Assassins<br /> <b>Pantheon: </b>Dodekatheon<br /> <b>Parent: </b>Diyonisos/Hades<br /> <b>Nature: </b>Bon Vivant/Competitor <br /> <br /> <b>Info: </b>Lypeos and Theraos are linked together more closely than any other pair of gods has ever been and to speak of one is to speak of the other inevitably. Their mother was a successful actress in her days, being called the &quot;Muse of Cinema&quot; by many and apparently rightfully so for not one but two Greek Gods took a liking to her beauty. And so both Diyonisos, God of Wine and Hades, Lord of the Underworld, approached the mortal in different guises, Diyonisos as a male stripper at her Bachelor Party, Hades as her soon-to-be Husband in the same night. And, unknowingly, she thus became pregnant with not one but two Scions of different gods. <br /> <br /> Fate, however, intervened and decided that only one Scion was to live. Diego Aramando was born a healthy and strong baby boy, while his half-brother Lysandros died before he was even born, strangled by his own umbirical cord. He was buried shortly after his birth and Diego never received word of his stillborn sibling. His parents agreed that it would be to his best. <br /> Diego Aramando grew up to be a handsome young man, a gifted actor and genius vintner who was both admired for his skills on the vineyard and his presence in front of the camera or in the round of the theater, never failing to amaze a crowd. He was equally known for his almost supernatural streak of accidents, however, which came to haunt him more than once. Whenever Diego took up a glass it would end up shattered on the floor, any tuxedo he donned would become tattered before he could undress again and whenever he turned on the radio it just started to air the 5-hour Justin Bieber special and the toggle button broke. Still, he lived a happy life, never being bitter over those &quot;Fun little things&quot; and hopped from Job to Job, working as a winegrower, a model, an actor and a male escort just to name a few. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Lysandros spent his first years quite literally in hell, being cradled by Persephone whenever she was around or shown the workings of the Tartatos by his father, who for some reason had taken pity on his infant soul - or maybe just saw it as a useful tool to execute his agenda. Lysandros didn't receive a new body, that was beyond what his father was able to do for him, but he got taken in and trained by the finest mortals that ever died. Combat, tactics and weaponry were taught to him like reading and writing and before other Scions even got their visitation he was already a well-versed killer, capable of overcoming any mortal enemy - and some supernatural ones as well. At least in theory. But he lacked a body to execute his will and that was where his brother came into the picture again. <br /> <br /> Diego received his visitation after a particularly smashed night, waking up in an apartment that clearly wasn't his own with a handsome young man who made pancakes - wearing nothing bot an apron. After a short series of misunderstandings, the man revealed himself to be Diegos real father, God of Wine, and that Diegos continous unlucky streak was in no small part thanks to him. But then again, so were his good looks, his stamina and his charismatic personality, so no hard feelings. Among the presents Diyonisos had gotten for his son was a small puch containing five coins which were called &quot;Oboli&quot;, originally intended as a token for Charon to do his job. Whenever he was in trouble, Diyonisos told him, he was to place one of those coins under his tongue and hope for the best. <br /> <br /> Naturally, those coins had been given to Diyonisos by Hades after a long night and allowed Lysandros to take over. Every time Diego put one of those coins in his mouth, Lysandros' Soul took over his body and was able to do as he pleased for six hours before he had to retread into the realms of the dead once more. And Diego was none the wiser, remembering nothing afterwards. <br /> Of course, he found out eventually and was shocked by the atrocities his brother had committed. For a long time he tried to ignore the issue, not swallowing those vile coins again and even throwing them away. But Lysandros found his ways into Diegos mind and finally managed to take him over by force, pushing his brothers soul out of his body. It took them three years to overcome their rivalry and finally get Lysandros a body of his own, a statue crafed by Pygmalion himself. <br /> <br /> Nowadays, Lypeos is the ideal picture of a greek man which short, curled hair, a perfectly toned body and dark complexion. He wears mostly loose clothing and is almost never seen alone, a cheerful crowd following him everywhere he goes. Also, he tends to break things a lot, although he has it under control by now. At least partially. <br /> <br /> Theraos on the other hand is a fearsome man, his face always hidden by a mask or shadows. He carries two guns and his signature weapon, gloves with razor-sharp fingernails, everywhere he goes. He passes unnoticed and kills silently, for he is the executive arm of Hades, getting those souls that have evaded his fathers grasp. He still uses Lypeos' mind for that end, sometimes, but they have a mutual understanding that what the other does furthers the agenda of the Dodekatheon - for now at least. <br /> <br /> <b>Associated Powers: </b>Epic Appearance, Epic Charisma, Epic Stamina, Arete, Chaos, Fertility / Epic Dexterity, Epic Perception, Epic Wits, Arete, Darkness, Death <br /> <b>Associated Abilities: </b>Art, Empathy, Fortitude, Larceny, Politics, Presence / Brawl, Command, Investigation, Marksmanship, Melee, Stealth <br /> <b>Rivals: </b>Hera; Horus, Loki, Quetzalcoatl, Susano-o, Baron Samedi / Hermes; Anubis, Vidar, Tezcatlipoca, Hachiman, Shango<br /> <br /> (Two NPCs of mine whom I made gods because I felt it was fun.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T14:03:17-08:00","id":769526,"title":"","content":"Guess what! I finally got my hands on <b>Scion: Hero</b> and <b>Scion: Demigod</b> yesterday. I should be able to make more appropriate characters now! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T11:42:03-08:00","id":770166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/690569-your-ascended-scions?p=769452#post769452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Very inspiring stuff]<br /> ..</div> </div> </div> </div>I love this background! Very clever and original!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T21:52:07-08:00","id":783928,"title":"","content":"<b>Soktes / Angelo DeManes</b><br /> God of lies, drought, mud, grain, and grudges. Former scion of Sobek.<br /> Where his father is god of the Nile, he is god of its banks and marshes. Where Sobek is god of amelioration, Soktes is god of outright lies, both for personal gain and relieving of others. He is wily and distrustful, but not blind to those in need. He is fierce to those who disrespect him and make of him an enemy, but as an ally he is just as great.<br /> <br /> Since his ascension, Soktes has become patron of spies, liars, orphans, drunks, and the personally wronged. His former followers, now a cult of worshippers, tattoo themselves with an image of a monitor lizard, the sacred animal of Soktes. They are instructed to right the wrongs of those who are broken or defeated, be they personal vendettas or legal battles. Not a single member is allowed to reveal their given name, instead living by an alias.<br /> <br /> As a hero, Angelo's first adventure led him to join a band, with whom he suffered through a grueling battle that cost them two members and a vicious defeat, earning them a band of enemies. Throughout his climb to godhood, Angelo would lose every member of his original band, enticing him to, upon finding the Black Feather Shroud they had sought for years, rend it to pieces. The relic Khopesh he gained from his visitation, Crocodile Tears, has evolved into the shape of a sickle, the tool of a farmer for harvesting grain.<br /> \u200b<br /> In his godly shape, Soktes takes the form of a tall, broad man with bronze skin and the head of a great lizard. He wears a great sash adorned in lapis and garnet, set with iron studs in the pattern of a monitor's skin. His kilt is dyed an earthy brown, the color of fresh mud or soil. In his right hand he holds his Sickle, and in his left he holds either a bundle of grain over his shoulder or else a great book, inked in many dialects and languages. While some believe that his attire leaves much to be desired, Soktes is never within earshot of those who would insult him.<br /> <br /> Soktes makes regular trips to the world, for varying reasons and jobs. Not the least of which being his continued hunt for the remaining members of the band that killed his fellows, all those years ago. He also maintains contacts with various seedy types, keeping tabs on the Titans and their supporters. In the world, Soktes takes the shape of a large man with a mysterious glint in his eye and an edge in his voice. He isn't off-putting, but puts those around him on edge, unwilling to make mistakes in his presence. He has occupied a multitude of positions, including CEO of an organized farming company, defense consultant, private investigator, captain of a river ferry, and leader of an underground spy ring.<br /> <br /> Scions of Soktes tend to be aloof and bad at maintaining personal relationships, due either to their difficulty in telling the whole truth, or because those around them tend to fall victim to a series of deadly happenings. They are the types who are skilled manipulators, but with no problem getting their hands dirty. Without fail, his scions hold onto grudges for a lifetime, be it their own or their enemy's. It isn't unlikely for them to end up in such positions as information brokers, criminal attorneys, and secret agents. Their time in most other positions tends to be short due to their loose relationship with the truth.<br /> <br /> <b>Powers</b>: Epic Manipulation, Epic Stamina, Epic Wits, Animal (Nile Monitor), Earth, Fertility, Heku, Justice, Water<br /> <b>Abilities</b>: Awareness, Control, Empathy, Politics, Stealth, Survival<br /> <b>Rivals</b>: Bast, Geb, Isis; Ares, Artemis, Frigg, Tyr, Manann\u00e1n Mac Lir, Quetzalcoatl<br /> <br /> (This was literally the first character I ever played in a scion campaign. We did *more or less* the long road to heaven campaign from the books, as well as several other offshoot campaigns of our own devising. In that first campaign, we had two of our characters die while Angelo here only barely survived. After that he made it his life's mission to take down our rival band, as well as destroy that damn shroud. We played scion for a while, with our band at the time finally reaching Godhood in our respective pantheons, and mine was the only character to survive the whole way through. This guy and I have gone through a lot together, is what I'm saying.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10163-toomuchjesus","name":"Toomuchjesus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T00:08:06-08:00","id":783971,"title":"","content":"(Might decide to add write ups for the rest of The Rising Stars later. What do you think? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Thaddeus Zurlo:</b> Scion of Zeus<br /> <br /> <b>AKA:</b> Thaddeus, Zurlo, The Cloud Prince<br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> God of hubris, vanity and the abuse of one's authority. As a Scion of Zeus, Thaddeus is a chip off the ol' block. As a mortal he was born and raised within the 1% community and was pretty much guaranteed to never run into financial problems. His family were business tycoons who had investments in multiple big name companies with a product in almost every household in the country. So when Thaddeus became old enough to become the new head of the family, he had more wealth than he could spend in a mortal life time. Unfortunately for those under Thaddeus' employ, he had practically zero sense of responsibility!<br /> <br /> While the middle class worked their asses off to keep the companies running smoothly, Thaddeus was spending millions of dollars on luxury cruises, first class flights around the world and taking narcotics so illegal than a common man would be jailed for life. Only once did his employees come close to taking him down when they started to suspect him of embezzlement and corruption. His real father, Zeus came to him and revealed his heritage while also exposing the identities of those who plotted against him. The Scion's immediate response was to smite the rebellious employees, sending compensation checks to their family along with his sympathies for their losses. His next immediate reaction was to snort coke off a hooker's tits and pretend he hadn't just committed mass murder to protect his lifestyle!<br /> <br /> After his visitation, Thaddeus became the leader of a Band of Scions called The Rising Stars, comprised entirely of Scions from the Dodekatheon. The other members in his band included a daughter of Poseidon, a daughter of Hades, a son of Hermes, a son of Hephaestus, and a son of Dionysus. Thaddeus conducted the Band like a group of divas who were accustomed to getting their way and who were never impressed by mortal attempts to please their ridiculously high expectations.<br /> <br /> <br /> Like his father Zeus, Thaddeus believes that his status alone gives him the authority to bend the rules, if not outright break them. He places very high expectations on those around him, but often at times fails to live up to his own standards. Those who call him out on his bullshit, however, tend to earn his wrath for speaking out of turn. For beings of Legend, this typically results in a severe beating. For mortals, it unsurprisingly ends with their deaths, as Zurlo is not very experienced at restraining himself.<br /> <br /> <br /> One of his most legendary accomplishments was during his Hero days, when Thaddeus managed to temporarily overthrow Zeus and convince the king of the gods not to punish him! After discovering an artifact known as the Black Feather Shroud and learning it could transfer a god's power into its wearer, Thaddeus used it to steal Zeus' power for himself, becoming the new King of the Gods for about 5 minutes. When the shroud was stolen away from him, Zeus' power returned and Thaddeus was reduced to a Hero again. Before Zeus could vaporize him on the spot, Thaddeus flew into a philosophical speech about how Zeus was Fated to be overthrown by one his own sons. According to Thaddeus, the prophecy had come true, although not in the way they had expected. Zeus was now free of his ancient Fate Bond and no longer had to worry about being usurped in the future! Reluctantly, Zeus acknowledge the wisdom in this and chose to spare his traitorous son, but not before giving him a death glare warning to never try that again. Years later, Thaddeus would earn his ascension to godhood through more legitimate methods.<br /> <br /> <br /> On his path to godhood, Zurlo accomplished many great deeds; He was trained in magic by the legendary Circe, he stopped the resurrection of Atlantis which would have destroyed the whole damn planet if it had been allowed to continue, Zeus granted him dominion over swans as a symbol of his virility (though only those who have studied Greek mythology would understand the reference), and when confronted by guilt for his past actions, he punched Satan in the face!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In his godly form, Zurlo looks like a younger version of Zeus, appearing to be in his early 30's. His hair is white as the clouds, but he doesn't have his father's beard. His eyes are electric blue and he often bares a smug grin while thinking of his past accomplishments. His skin is flawlessly unblemished and he bares the uncanny physique of an Olympian, wearing the traditional garb of the ancient Greeks.<br /> <br /> <br /> The only reason Zurlo comes to the mortal world anymore is for some rest and relaxation when he has a free moment away from the Titan war. When he visits, he makes a stop to one of his many bank accounts, draws out a few million dollars, then throws the vacation of a life time. Often these vacations involve unprotected sex and bastard children. But due to his selfish life style, there is an estimated 1 in 10 chance these children will be granted a visitation. After all, raising kids is expensive and annoying, so he'll only bother with the best of the litter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Powers: </b>Epic Manipulation, Epic Strength, Epic Stamina, Arete, Sky, Justice, Magic, Animal (Swan)<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities: </b>Command, Politics, Presence, Brawl, Athletics, Academics<br /> <br /> <b>Rivals:</b> Hera, Horus, Set, Loki, Tezcatlipoca<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Additional Notes:</b> While Zurlo has many enemies, there are only a handful of Gods who he actually considers to be his rivals. This list is primarily comprised of those who he feels wish to interfere with his high society life style and expect him to take a more mature approach to things. As a Scion of Zeus, it is absolutely no surprise that Hera would find herself on his short list. The other positions are filled by Gods of Fate, Justice and Disease, all things which can ruin a good time while he's throwing his latest party. Loki is also on that list because he's just an ass hole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-13-2015, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T21:58:50-08:00","id":784535,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Ophelia Leventis:</b> Scion of Poseidon<br /> <br /> <b>AKA:</b> Tamer of Beasts, Queen of the Minotaur<br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> Goddess of animal husbandry, wrestling and livestock. At first glance, Ophelia would be the last person you would expect to be a child of Poseidon. She grew up on a ranch, with the nearest ocean being at least a hundred miles away. But what is often overlooked was Poseidon was also the God of horses. Ophelia may not have had her father's affinity towards water, but she was very skilled at handling animals, and that made her worthy in her own right.<br /> <br /> Ophelia's visitation came during her first cattle drive without her parents around to assist her. The 200 heads of cattle she was leading were suddenly attacked by a Cyclops who intended to steal the herd for his own, and was willing to kill Ophelia to get it. When Poseidon intervened and gave a brief explanation of the situation, Ophelia wrestled the Cyclops to the ground, binding him like a subdued calf. Some time after that, she joined up with The Rising Stars, a Band of Greek Scions lead by Thaddeus Zurlo. Afterward, she began to make a Legend for herself by taming a multitude of dangerous animals, bringing them under the control of the Gods.<br /> <br /> During her journeys, Ophelia gained dominion over a variety of different animals, but the beast that she is most famous for is the bull. While on a journey to Crete, Ophelia encountered a horde of Minotaur who attempted to use her to satisfy their perverse urges. Rather than kill them all in self defense, Ophelia merely subdued them with a display of force. Afterward, she branded her initials into their hides and claimed them as her slaves. In recognition of this deed, Poseidon conferred upon her the title of &quot;Queen of the Minotaur&quot; for bringing one of his errant creations under control.<br /> <br /> Ophelia is one of the few members in the Dodekatheon who does not look like the perfect image of a human. In fact, she looks more like the animals she is so closely tied with. In her full godly form, Ophelia resembles a female Minotaur (the first of her kind, perhaps). Her body is anthropomorphic standing upright with the arms and torso of a human, but possessing the head, tail, legs and fur of a cow. Four breasts adorn her exposed upper body while a cotton skirt covers her from waist to knees. She is noticeably more muscular than is typically common among women, likely due to a life time of wrestling dangerous animals, such as Titanspawn.<br /> <br /> Although the Dodekatheon is normally unkind towards inhuman deities, Ophelia has earned a modicom of respect from her peers. Thanks to her, the Dodekatheon have obtained a variety of powerful and dangerous war beasts to throw against the Titan invasion, all of which she tamed by proving she was stronger than them. If the Dodekatheon believe the bipedal cow is an embarassment to their ranks, they have so far chosen to hold their tongues. This may change, however, once they feel they no longer require her services in the war.<br /> <br /> Both as a mortal and as a goddess, Ophelia has displayed the personality of a tomboy. She enjoys hard work and dirty jobs, offering no more complaints than any man might to perform suck a task. As a result, many of her worshipers see her as a female empowerment figure. When staying in the mortal World, she has been the traditional rancher, a self defense coach, a dominatrix, a proffesional wrestler, an obedience school instructor, and a tattoo artist.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Powers:</b> Epic Charisma, Epic Strength, Animal (Sheep), Animal (Bovine), Animal (Pig), Animal (Horse), Earth, Arete<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities:</b> Animal Ken, Control, Fortitude, Thrown, Brawl, Marksmanship<br /> <br /> <b>Rivals:</b> Ares, Freyr, Artemis, Aphrodite, Xipe Totec<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Additional Notes:</b> When traveling through the divine realms, Ophelia is accompanied by 1-3 of her Minotaur followers. The enslaved creatures have the initials O.L branded into their hide, marking them as property of Ophelia Leventis. She wisely keeps the Minotaur out of sight when traveling the mortal World, however.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-12-2015, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T19:27:09-08:00","id":785127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/690569-your-ascended-scions?p=784535#post784535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Ophelia Leventis:</b> Scion of Poseidon<br /> <br /> <b>Powers:</b> Epic Charisma, Epic Strength, Animal (Sheep), Animal (Bovine), Animal (Pig), Animal (Horse), Earth, Arete<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities:</b> Animal Ken, Control, Fortitude, Thrown, Melee, Marksmanship<br /> <br /> <b>Rivals:</b> Ares, Freyr, Artemis, Aphrodite, Xipe Totec<br /> <br /> <br /> </span></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm surprised one of her associated abilities isn't Brawl, considering she's a goddess of strength and wrestling.<br /> Just a thought, though<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10163-toomuchjesus","name":"Toomuchjesus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T19:31:44-08:00","id":785131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toomuchjesus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/690569-your-ascended-scions?p=785127#post785127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm surprised one of her associated abilities isn't Brawl, considering she's a goddess of strength and wrestling.<br /> Just a thought, though</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Woops, you're right. I accidentally put Melee instead of Brawl. Editing that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-12-2015, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T23:13:03-08:00","id":785203,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Melody Kondos:</b> Scion of Hades<br /> <br /> <b>AKA:</b> Melodia<br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> Goddess of eulogies and funerals, Princess of the Underworld and guide to lost souls. Born to a family of jewelers, Melody is no stranger to the art of fine craftsmanship. But although she was trained by her parents in the manufacturing of shiny trinkets and accessories, her true passion was music, particularly singing. When she wasn't helping out her family's business, she would practice singing, entertaining fantasies of one day becoming famous and joining a band.<br /> <br /> Maybe it was nostalgic memories of Orpheus from so long ago, but Hades was most pleased with Melody's voice. One day, while Melody was finally earning recognition for her musical talent, Hades gave her a visitation, stealing her away from the talent scouts and agencies that would have exploited her for personal gain. Melody was already an exceptionally talented singer, but once her power of Arete began to manifest, her voice was nearly hypnotic.<br /> <br /> In fact, it was her enchanting songs that lead to her now holding the position she does in the Underworld. With the Titan's prison destroyed, souls were no longer instinctively drawn to the Underworld after their deaths. Thus, Melody took on the role of luring the dead to their final resting place, using her music to ease their regrets and help the dead find peace. It may not be as effective as a mind controlling ghost magnet in the center of the realm, but it works, none the less.<br /> <br /> Ironically, Melody got her wish and ended up joining a Band, just not the kind she was hoping for. After her visitation, she was recruited into The Rising Stars, a group of Scions that consisted entirely of Dodekatheon children. With the addition of her in the group, the Band now had a child of Zeus, Poseidon and Hades working together, a very powerful combitination. Being more of an entertainer at heart, Melody was the physically weakest member of The Rising Stars, preferring to solve her problems through words if at all possible. When she did have to resort to violence, she heavily relied on her Birthrights to accomplish the goal.<br /> <br /> <br /> In her full Godly form, Melody appears as a hauntingly beautiful woman in her mid twenties. Her hair is black as a moonless night and her eyes are emerald green. Although her complexion is flawless, she has the unusual characteristic of pale gray skin, as if coated in ashes. She primarily wears a hooded, black robe and often seen carrying a harp or a lyre as her preferred instrument. Her voice is melodic in tone and her disposition is compassionate and welcoming unless given a reason to become hostile.<br /> <br /> As the escort of lost souls, Melody is primarily focused with combating the restless dead and the Titans who control them. She has battled some of the most powerful spectres, zombies, vampires and whatever else continues to haunt the World after it's demise. Laying their bodies to rest, and cleansing their souls of madness.<br /> <br /> When visiting the mortal world, Melody takes on disguises that suit her role in the Underworld. She has been a singer at funerals, an exorcist, a mortician and a grief counselor. Sometimes, when she's feeling nostalgic, she takes the form of a jewelry maker to honor the memory of her mortal parents.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Powers:</b> Epic Charisma, Epic Appearance, Arete, Death, Earth, Psychopomp<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities:</b> Art , Command, Presence, Stealth, Craft, Empathy<br /> <br /> <b>Rivals:</b> Apollo, Thoth, Baron Samedi, Baldur, Hel, Isanami</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T20:16:36-08:00","id":786467,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>(4 down, 2 more to go)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Karena Kollias:</b> Scion of Haphaestus<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> Even before accepting her role as a Scion, Karena was at least partially familiar with Thaddeus Zurlo, because she worked at one of his family's corporations. As a mortal, Karena worked as a robotics developer, helping to create the world of tomorrow by building more sophisticated machinery. When Hephaestus learned that Thaddeus was putting a band together and that they had prior association with his daughter, he decided to give her a visitation and encourage her to join up. Following her father's advice, she became a member of The Rising Stars and traveled with her &quot;boss&quot; on their path to godhood together.<br /> <br /> As a Scion, Karena's inventions went from revolutionary to something approaching the realm of science fiction. It was not long before she discovered the art of combining technology with supernatural energy, creating machines that were just as much magical as they were scientific. Within a a year of carrying out her Scion duties, she had reached a level of genius no ordinary mortal could match, and she knew it! Eventually she grew bored with the mortal's limited grasp of scientific possibilities and devoted her research to the war against the Titans and their forces. Creating autonomous war machines to engage Titanspawn without having to risk the lives of valued agents. Those of a more warrior mindset would brand her a coward, but she sees them as primitive and ignorant. The days of hand to hand combat ended hundreds of years ago. War isn't fought with swords and bows and trebuchets anymore, it's fought with automatic rifles, incendiary grenades and unmanned drones. If they want to attack the Titans with rocks and sticks, they're free to do so, but this is a war Karena intends to win!<br /> <br /> <br /> Sadly, Karena's destiny as a Scion condemned her to suffer a similar fate to that of her father. She is crippled, her arms being torn from their sockets by an angry Cyclops during her Hero days. Refusing to allow his daughter's talent to be lost forever, Hephaestus implanted her with mechanical arms which doubled as Relics for her godly powers. Despite her new limbs being vastly superior to her old ones, she is still quite bitter over their loss and has developed an intense dislike for all Cyclopes who have not been cowed into submission to the Dodekatheon.<br /> <br /> <br /> In her full Godly form, Karena takes the form of a beautiful woman with curly red hair, deep blue eyes and mechanical arms forged out of some kind of unidentified golden alloy. She wears a traditional Greek tunic, but often wears an open lab coat over it to remind herself she's not living in ancient times. While wearing the coat, the only part of her artificial limbs that remain visible are the hands, but the implants actually start around the shoulders and continue down from there.<br /> <br /> <br /> Karena doesn't visit the mortal world too often anymore, as she feels it is too primitive to keep up with her aspiring genius. When she does visit, it is because she has been seized by inspiration and feels compelled to share her new invention with the World. Unfortunately for the World, these inventions are so highly advanced, that modern society is not prepared to handle them. So their blueprints are classified to the public and being worked on secretly in a government research facility. Hopefully mankind will be mature enough to handle them once their developments are complete.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Powers: </b>Epic Intelligence, Epic Stamina, Epic Wits, Arete, Fire, Earth, Mystery, Guardian<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities:</b> Craft, Science, Art, Control, Marksmanship, Thrown<br /> <br /> <b>Rivals: </b>Ares, Ptah, Huitzilopochtli, Hachiman, Damballa</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-03-2016, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T14:17:30-08:00","id":791089,"title":"","content":"<b>Eustis Baros:</b> Scion of Dionysus<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> God of social anarchy and sexual freedom; as well as the estranged lover to Drakon (a fellow Bandmate). Even in his mortal years, Eustis was already showing himself to be his father's son when he decided to pursue a career in the adult film industry. Working his way up the ranks, he eventually found himself in the director's chair and went onto produce award winning films, the titles of which shall not be mentioned here! Life was looking good for young Eustis until the day of his visitation, which set into motion a chain of events turning him into one of the most frustrating beings in the world.<br /> <br /> Eustis was visited by Dionysus with a warning that one of his actors was a servant of Pan who was going to try and convert him to the exile's cause. Awakening his Scion heritage, Dionysus left his son to clean up the mess himself as he had other matters to attend to. It turns out &quot;servant&quot; meant &quot;Scion&quot; in this case and when Eustis confronted the agent, it turned into quite a heated battle, with Eustis just barely coming out on top of the situation. A few weeks later, he managed to join up with The Rising Stars as one of their most volatile members.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even before his ascension to godhood, Eustis has always been a Rebel. He despises expectations and scoffs as social norms, instead preferring freedom and expression over conformity. As a Scion, Eustis made it his mission to bring about change to the social order. Sometimes this change was for the better, toppling centuries of outdated prejudice and superstition. Sometimes this change was disastrous, plunging society into self destructive anarchy. He is not particularly skilled in battle, but a silver tongue can accomplish more than any mere sword. He slinks through the background, whispering into the ears of kings and commoners alike, encouraging them to break from tradition and express themselves regardless of what others may think.<br /> <br /> <br /> In his full godly form, Eustis appears as an overweight man just shy of obesity and dressed in ancient Greek fashion. His hair is black and braided into a pony tail which he often drapes over one of his shoulders as his preferred hair style. Despite his bulk, Eustis' skin appears to be clean of the usual blemishes that comes with such a body type, instead being clean and smooth to the touch. It is also worth noting, that he never wears undergarments, making his tunic more revealing that others might feel comfortable with.<br /> <br /> <br /> As a member of the Dodekatheon, Eustis does not recognize biological Scions. This is not because he is a virgin (far from it, actually), but rather due in part to his own preference. Eustis is homosexual and will only (willingly) take men as his lovers. Because of this, he prefers to adopt unclaimed Scions rather than conceive his own. When or if Eustis does produce a child of his own, he refuses to take responsibility for it, claiming that the child's mother likely date raped him to make it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Powers: </b>Epic Charisma, Epic Stamina, Epic Manipulation, Arete, Chaos, Health, Animal (Swine)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Abilities: </b>Art, Empathy, Presence, Athletics, Politics, Larceny<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rivals:</b> Aphrodite, Hera, Zeus, Set, Damballa<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T17:36:39-08:00","id":791174,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Fr\u00f3\u00f0i</b></u><br /> <b>Role: </b>God of Prophecy <br /> <b>Pantheon: </b>The Aesir<br /> <b>Parent: </b>Odin<br /> <b>Nature: </b>Visionary<br /> <br /> <b>Info: </b>Fr\u00f3\u00f0i was born in Norway as Njord Sigurdsson, as the spouse of a successful businesswoman who had a short but passionate affair with a Swedish estate agent who had lost one eye in a hunting accident. His mother, Sigurd Halvarsdottir, didn't love Njord. In fact she despised him, for his father had left her just shortly before he had been born and he served as a living remainder of that. While the boy never failed to receive proper education and a home, he found himself lacking attention and care and thus drifted towards many occult sects and opinions, making well-versed in both Nordic Religions and Hermeticism, among other things. He still was terribly angry with the world at large, however, and thus joined a spiritual successor of the Thule Society. <br /> <br /> Being forced not only by his criminal record that piled up during his time in the neo-fascistic brotherhood but also by his mother threatening to cut off his financial support soon he moved to Germany, learning the language much faster than even he had believed possible and decided to study German philology, Religious Studies and History in Berlin. He had to support himself, of course, earning money by working in a library and, occasionally, reading Tarot Cards to rich idiots. He was sixteen years old at that time, having skipped quite a few grades. <br /> <br /> As Fate willed it, Njord met his family during one of his library jobs. His boss had soon realized that the boy had a knack for finding old and valuable books that sold well to a certain clientle, not knowing that this clientle mostly consisted of young Njord himself. He had sent him to an antique store in the centre of Berlin where an old man was supposedly sitting on a proverbial goldmine. This old man turned out to be Njords father, Odin, and he told his son exactly what he was. He also foretold his future and saw great deeds there, skipping on only one detail. A detail that hit Njord on his way home in the shape of an out-of-control truck which almost ran the boy over. Njord could save himself, but his eyes he could not. Two shards of a nearby window hit him in the face, blinding him forever. <br /> <br /> Filled with regret over what had happened, Njord decided to get back at Odin for knowing. He guessed, correctly as Odin himself confirmed, that the All-Father knew fully well about his impending blindness but chose not to warn him for it was inevitable. Not content with this explanation, Njord decided to learn the ways of Fate and how to bend them to his will. <br /> During the next years he grew more and more prominent both as an eccentric owner of an Occult Store and a seer who sometimes made disturbingly accurate predictions. After predicting almost every event of the year 2013 correctly, including several figures such as people to die during a Hurricane, he decided to set out to further is Legend, assuming that he needed more prominence to become a god. <br /> <br /> Nowadays, he is Fr\u00f3\u00f0i the Blind, who yet sees more than anyone, safe perhaps for the Norns. Living in a small cave consiting of dead roots from dead Yggdrasil, he is often visited for his wisdom and knowledge of the hidden workings of Fate, but equally feared for the same reasons. Yet, his goal still remains unfulfilled: Changing the destiny of the Gods themselves to finally make his father admit that he was wrong. It is a big goal, but Fr\u00f3\u00f0i is certain of his abilities. <br /> <br /> <b>Associated Powers: </b>Epic Charisma, Epic Intelligence, Epic Perception, Jotunblut, Magic, Mystery, Prophecy, Star<br /> <b>Associated Abilities: </b>Academics, Awareness, Empathy, Investigation, Occult, Presence<br /> <b>Rivals: </b>Odin; Bastet, Apollo, Tezcatlipoca, Tsuki-Yomi, Legba","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T20:24:05-08:00","id":791257,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Whew, finally done!</b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Drakon Riga:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Scion of Hermes</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> One could say that even before his visitation, Drakon was already a legend in the making. From a young age, Drakon had a desire to get out and explore the world, like his mysterious father who was nowhere to be found. In an effort to track him down, Drakon joined the secret services when he became old enough, hoping to gain access to their information in between missions. Of course being a god, it would have been impossible for him to actually locate Hermes, had he not wanted to be found.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">To call it a visitation is a tad inaccurate, for it was Drakon who came to visit Hermes. Or rather came to arrest him as the trickster God was assuming one of his mortal disguises at the time. It failed, of course, resulting in Drakon being caught in a very elaborate death trap, with Hermes explaining his true origins to him and then promptly leaving him to his fate. With his Scion powers now awakened, Drakon managed to escape the trap, but his father was already long gone and Thaddeus Zurlo was there waiting for him with a job offer. Drakon accepted the proposal, joining The Rising Stars and completing the group.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">During his time as a Scion, Drakon was the ideal super spy. He was charming, he was quick witted, he was a certified bad ass, and he was virtually impossible to kill with anything short of open combat. He's lost count of how many times his enemies have left him in a death trap, only for him to escape using some convoluted plan or gadget that Karena whipped up for him.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">In his full godly form, Drakon is a very handsome man with sharp, angular features, wavy brown hair and deep blue eyes. He prefers to dress in three piece suits even when on Olympus and carries a variety of accessories which are actually Relics custom built for his line of work. These accessories change by the day, but commonly include a pocket watch, cuff links, a monocle and a broach.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Although Drakon is sexually involved with Eustis, he is not strictly homosexual and sometimes conceives Scions of his own. Luckily for him, Eustis isn't as hung up about the who monogamy thing as the rest of the pantheon, which (usually) prevents him from taking vengeance out on the innocent Scions.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The children of Drakon share their father's gifts of being both socially graceful and physically capable. They often find themselves joining covert organizations, operating behind the enemy lines or even within their very ranks to take down the Titans while their attention is turned elsewhere.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Powers:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Epic Dexterity, Epic Intelligence, Epic Wits, Epic Charisma, Arete, Star</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Abilities:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Athletics, Brawl, Stealth, Awareness, Survival, Marksmanship</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T16:08:28-08:00","id":795154,"title":"","content":"<b>Kollsvein:</b> Scion of Loki<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>AKA:</b> Kollsvein Fenrisson, Alex Rutfol<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> A God of hunting and an adoptive Scion of Loki. Kollsvein is Loki's grandchild, born to a same sex couple who used a donation from a sperm bank to conceive a child. What they were unaware of going in was the donation came from the dread wolf, Fenris. Loki had placed it among the others as both a prank and an experiment to see whether his monstrous children were capable of producing Scions. Much to his delight, it worked and nine months later the couple gave birth to Alex Rutfol.<br /> <br /> <br /> Much like the Fenris who indirectly spawned him, Alex grew rapidly during childhood. He entered puberty nearly two years early and it hit him like a truck.By the time he was 15, he was almost 6 feet tall and growing a beard. He also exhibited a lot of pent up frustration and continuously challenged other kids his age to physical contests which he unsurprisingly won. That was when Loki decided to pay him a visit at home, revealing both to Alex and to his parents that he was the one who had donated the sample, though he kept the more exact details about where it came from to himself until he and Alex were alone.<br /> <br /> <br /> After learning the truth about himself and reading the prophecy of Ragnarok, Alex developed feelings of apathy towards everything. Yes, the world is doomed, but the prophecy also says that the surviving gods will create a new world to replace the old one. If the world is going to be reborn, does it really matter if the Titans destroy this one? Alex doesn't think so, and instead has decided to have as much fun as possible before the end of the world happens and (almost) everybody dies.<br /> <br /> <br /> Rather than spend his time attempting to preserve the world, Alex (going by his mortal name at the time) sought to increase his legend through trials of skill and strength. He did not battle the Titanspawn because he felt what they did was wrong, he fought them because he wanted to prove he could. Each victory strengthened his reputation and his sense of accomplishment. Unfortunately for Loki, however, Alex was also shown to display Fenris' sense of cunning and was able to recognize a bad deal when it was presented to him. When faced with an open challenge, Alex demanded special assurances to guarantee the competition was fair. If it was not, his dishonorable opponent was sure to lose a hand (or some other body part) for daring to trick him.<br /> <br /> <br /> One of Kollsvein's most noticeable characteristics is his wolf fetish, being fascinated with the creatures to the point of having mastered the Animal Purview. Both as a Scion and as a God, he bore no animosity towards the Fenrir as long as they did not attack him first. The more paranoid members of the Aesir fear that Kollsvein is going to side with the Titans at the time of Ragnarok, perhaps even helping Fenris break the binds that have kept him subdued for thousands of years. Alas, they do not have any magical thread to restrain their newest member and even if they did, he is likely to not fall for the same trick.<br /> <br /> <br /> In his true godly form, Kollsvein looks more like some ancient savage. He is very large, standing around 7 feet tall and with powerfully built muscles. He is estimated to weigh around 250 pounds, though has not been properly weighed in. He is also very hairy, sporting thick patches of body hair on his chest, forearms, face and shins. His eyes are bright green and his hair is dark black in color. His moustache is braided on both sides and he has a third braid in the center of his beard. He wears traditional viking garb, fashioned out of wolf pelts, a constant reminder of his ancestry.<br /> <br /> <br /> Scions of Kollsvein are noticeably rare in number. His viewpoint on Ragnarok has done little to stress the importance of giving visitations to his offspring. Instead, he passes them off to his grandfather who is all too happy to acquire free pawns in his grand schemes. When he does choose to accept responsibility for such a child, they often exhibit a sense of invincibility, overcoming many physical trials that other Scions deem impossible. Watching his Scions prevail against stacked odds brings great pleasure to Kollsvein, who raises a mug in their honor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Associated Powers:</b> Epic Manipulation, Epic Strength, Epic Wits, Epic Stamina, Jotunblut, Chaos, Fire, Health, Animal (Wolf)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Abilities:</b> Survival, Empathy, Brawl, Animal Ken, Fortitude, Stealth","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-05-2016, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T06:29:13-08:00","id":797310,"title":"","content":"Last One for a While. I'm planning an idea for a group of corrupted / evil Scions soon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wenhua Shizhe:</b> Scion of Sun Wukong<br /> <br /> <b>Role:</b> Goddess of Immigration<br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> Wenhua Shizhe, or &quot;Bringer of Culture&quot; is one of the rare members of the Celestial Bureaucracy who was not raised in Chinese surroundings. In fact, she's not even of Chinese ethnicity with the exception of her father being a member of their pantheon. Born and raised in America, Wenhua's mortal name was <i>Hailey Witt</i>. From an early age, she possessed a wander lust and voiced her desire to travel all over the world some day. Social studies was her favorite subject in school, learning the history and customs of foreign nations, which she took as a means of preperation for her journey one day. Unfortunately reality so rarely often lives up to fantasy. By the time she was 19 and graduated from school, she came to realize that her job had not provided nearly enough financial income for a trip across the world. That was when her heavenly father came to her and revealed the truth.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sun Wukong told Hailey that if she wanted to travel the world, all she had to do was start walking. After overcoming the initial shock of a large, talking monkey claiming to be her father, she decided to take up his advice and set out on her journey two days later, having quit her job when her last paycheck came in. As of that moment, she was technically a hobo, sleeping wherever she could find shelter and eating wherever she could find sustenance. It was far from the glamorous journey she had imagined growing up, but the machinations of Fate kept her going forward whenever she considered turning back.<br /> <br /> <br /> To this day, both Wenhua and Sun Wukong affectionately refer to her rise to godhood as the &quot;Journey to the East&quot; in parallel to Sun Wukong's own adventures. During her time as Hailey Witt, she traveled almost entirely by foot from America to China, encountering many Titanspawn plots and challenges along the way. By the time she became a demigod, she arrived in Brazil, to which she was forced to take a ship to the next continent over. Afterwhich, she made her way towards China, crossing through many small countries in the process.<br /> <br /> <br /> As a goddess, Wenhua Shizhe is part of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs who are tasked with dealing with outside cultures and ethnic minorities. Wenhua's job is to bring the teachings of China to the &quot;uncivilized barbarians&quot; that is the rest of the world. As a goddess of immigration, she is technically supposed to teach her fellow deities the ways of foreign cultures, but in practice the Celestial Bureaucracy has little regard for such things given their high stance on Chinese customs and values. When they do listen, it is usually in an effort to learn more about potential weaknesses or to use as proof of the superiority of Chinese culture throughout the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> Perhaps it is because Wenhua is not actually Chinese or perhaps it is in reverence to her divine father (possibly both), but Wenhua Shizhe does not take a human form when spending time in supernatural realms. Instead, her godly form takes the appearance of an anthropomorphic spider monkey of great size. Her limbs and body are proportionate to those of a human and she stands on her hind legs in a bipedal posture. Her body is mostly covered in red fur with some black around the paws, face and tail. Her clothing (at least in this form) is minimalistic, providing just enough to cover her modesty. When asked why she doesn't dress more appropriately for a woman, she kindly suggests that you try wearing an entire outfit when you're covered in fur.<br /> <br /> <br /> When dealing with the mortal World, Wenhua always takes the form of a foreigner who sympathizes with Chinese culture. Sometimes she serves as an educator or a translator for those planning to visit China. Other times she personally escorts foreigners on their own journey to the east, being the captain of a transport ship, an airline pilot or even just a cross country bus driver. Although her official role is to indoctrinate the barbarians to Chinese ways, she secretly enjoys learning about new cultures as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> Due to her appointed role, Wenhua refuses to have Scions with Chinese men, instead preferring to take foreigners as her lovers. Many within the beauracy have voiced their displeasure that she is sharing her divine ichor with barbarians, but she has tantively explained her actions as placing Bureaucracy Scions on foreign soil and giving China a foothold in those countries. What she does not reveal is her plan to diversify the pantheon by elevating the &quot;barbarians&quot; to godhood within the xenophobic Bureaucracy<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Associated Powers:</b> Epic Dexterity, Epic Strength, Epic Manipulation, Animal (Monkeys), Taiyi, Psychopomp, Earth<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Abilities:</b> Survival, Larceny, Athletics, Politics, Brawl, Investigation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-31-2015, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T02:00:24-08:00","id":815316,"title":"","content":"<b>Haldris: </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Scion of Hades</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Previously: Theo (Theophilus) DeMarcus</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Role: </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">God of Murder, Sacrifice, and Redemption</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Unlike his father, Haldris is neither patient nor contemplative in his plans. He is direct, excitable, and quick to action. He makes no move halfway, and leaves no business unfinished. That is not to say he is unintelligent or naive, simply that when he knows what must be done, it will be he who sees it through. As God of murder as well as redemption, Haldris plays a key role in the end of many lives, as well as seeing sinners brought back to justice.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As a mortal man, Theo was a homicide detective in Chicago, a city which guaranteed both job security and sleepless nights for him. When his mother was murdered in her own home, Theo was met at the scene by a tall, gaunt man who turned out to be his long lost father, known only by the checks that rolled in each month until his eighteenth birthday. After introductions, Hades laid out clear instructions to find those who did this to his once love, and bring them to justice however he was able. Not long after completing this mission, Theo joined his first band, and quickly made a name for himself by killing two Norse children of the wolf Fenris in as many days.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Theo eventually left his Band, wandering the world instead, returning restless dead to their respective destinations. In his travels he found himself in his own Underworld, and happened upon the shears of Atropos herself, later claiming them as his own birthright after the goddess reclaimed her ability over Fate. This became an onyx blade of terrible power which he continues to wield with devastating skill. Through this journeying he found he enjoyed sending the living to their final end as much as those already perished, and so became a talented warrior in addition to a skilled ppsychopomp.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">After his ascension, Haldris became gaunt and pale like his father, though not as thin. He appears athletic and youthful, though his eyes are those of a man of many lifetimes, even appearing as empty sockets at times. His hair is raven black, and falls neatly to his shoulders. Instead of a traditional toga, he wears a cloak made from the water of Styx itself, fashioned for him by the goddess Hecate. It is gray and any who look upon it long enough begin to make out the faces of tortured souls trapped in the fabric, fleeting as a trick of the eyes. He is never without his relic blade, which is able to change its shape to meet his needs, with the exception of always being black as the grave, and carrying a lethal edge.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">His trips to the world are always brief and direct, and almost never for recreation. On the off chance he has an extended stay, it would likely be in the form of some sort of authority figure with access to death records. It would not be out of the question for him to take the role of prison warden, psychiatrist, or AA/NA coordinator, as a way to bring those who have fallen from grace to recovery.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Scions of Haldris are quick to action, and quicker to violence. They are able to immediately and efficiently size up the best solution to a problem, whether it be through fighting or negotiation. His children are rare, but those he has, he maintains a fixed role for within their lives. His gifts to them are practical and directed toward their individual needs, but his direction is firm, and he is quick to set his children right when he sees them heading down the wrong path.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Associated Powers:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Epic Dexterity, Epic Wits, Arete, Death, Earth, Justice, Magic, Psychopomp</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Abilities:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Awareness, Empathy, Marksmanship, Melee, Occult, Presence</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10163,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10163-toomuchjesus","user":"Toomuchjesus","date":". 01-24-2016, 05:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10163-toomuchjesus","name":"Toomuchjesus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T05:31:05-08:00","id":815374,"title":"","content":"<b>Myrminki:</b> Scion of Hera and Gaia<br /> <br /> Previously: Kyle Junior<br /> <br /> <b>Role:</b> Avatar of Terra representing survival.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> Yet another example of the very long list of enemies created through the Dodekatheon's own hubris. Born under the name Kyle Junior, he was to be a Scion of Hera. But when Zeus found out about his wife's infidelity, he was furious and targeted the bastard for his revenge. On the night Hera was planning to visit him, Zeus sent forth a thunder storm that burned Kyle's house down, killing his mortal parents and burning him across 70% of his body. Hera was also forced to renounce her claim to him, lest she provoke Zeus further. But Kyle would be miraculously saved from a life as a cripple. Not by the Gods, but by the Titans; for he was visited that night in the hospital by Gaia, appearing in his dreams to explain she had saved him from the flames and offered him greater benefits if he would merely serve her. Kyle agreed and woke up in bed to find he had regained most of his motor skills and brain functions, as well as having his Scion powers awakened.<br /> <br /> Though he was only 16 years old at the time of his visitation, Kyle displayed a surprisingly high gift for coordinating others. Joining a band of other Scions who had sided with Terra, he demonstrated his skill by leading 20 mercenaries into battle and later Myrmidons as his powers continued to grow. The carapace armor granted to him by Hera caused his other bandmates to refer to him as the &quot;Ant King&quot; first as a joke, and then more seriously as his Legend continued to grow. Over time, Kyle began to accept the title and even fashion himself around it. During his rise to apotheosis, he became increasingly ant-like both in form and in function.<br /> <br /> After achieving godhood, Kyle allowed himself to be absorbed completely by the essence of Terra and was reborn as one of its avatars. Now going by the name of Myrminki, he embodies the concept of survival, when species of animals conquer and control their environment. He is the king of all species of ants, with every queen of every colony serving as his harem. As an Avatar, Myrminki has one goal in mind for the World.<br /> <br /> To conquer and control<br /> <br /> With his army of ants, he marches upon the World seeking to assimilate others into his hive. Those taken as slaves become Myrmidons, those found unworthy serve as food for the billions of insects he commands! Territories which are controlled by Myrminki are easily recognized, just look for the impossibly large ant mounds!<br /> <br /> <br /> Myrminki can take three forms all of which are styled after the ant. He can appear as a regular sized ant, or a gigantic one of near typhonian size. But his most common form is the bipedal, four armed ant man, which he uses for associating with people or battling agents of the Gods. While in this form, Myrminki's body is covered in a protective coating of chitinous armor, with three fingered claws on each of his four hands. His head is that of an ant, scaled to proportion with his man sized body and sporting wicked mandibles from his mouth. As befitting of a &quot;royal&quot; ant's station, he also possesses a set of gossamer wings allowing him to take to the air when when he so desires, giving him the advantage of mobility over his more grounded foes.<br /> <br /> <br /> As an Avatar, Myrminki no longer functions the same way as regular Scions in terms of ability and skill. However, prior to apotheosis, Kyle's specialized in the use of the Animal (ant), Fertility and Earth purviews and these continue to remain his favorites after becoming a Titan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-24-2016, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T07:41:22-08:00","id":815438,"title":"","content":"<br /> <b>Rutfol:</b> Scion of Loki<br /> <br /> <b>Role:</b> Avatar of Terra symbolizing the ecosystem<br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> Many of Loki's Scions are known to join the Titan side of the war, but most are hunted down because of this. Rutfol is one of the rare few who managed to survive and went onto become ever more powerful. As a Scion, Rutfol believed he could form a truce between Terra and humanity by turning the entire population of earth into therianthropes. Obviously his plans were stopped, but that didn't stop Rutfol from attempting new ways to forcefully control mankind's evolution.<br /> <br /> As his Legend grew, Rutfol's attempts for a peaceful resolution to the war became more and more unstable as his desperation increased. He began to grow less concerned with humanity's survival, and more focused on assimilating it back into the hands of nature. As long as Terra was happy with the results, humanity didn't have to be wiped out completely.<br /> <br /> Upon becoming an avatar for Terra, Rutfol now symbolizes the echosystem as a whole. He is the food chain that presents the circle of life in its most primal form. Technology is an abomination, one that allows weaker life forms to rise above their station and throw the echosystem into chaos. If he is to restore the balance of nature, he must destroy all traces of human civilization, plunging them back to the stone age from whence they came. <br /> <br /> Wherever he goes, Rutfol takes the form of the apex predator for that echosystem. He is rules the echosystem, after all, so it only makes sense he would be at the top of the food chain. When traveling in Terra, these predators are often of monstrous size to compete with the typhonian beasts that roam the land. <br /> <br /> Rutfol's human form is a shadow of what it once was. Before his apotheosis, he was a doctor possessed of supernatural intelligence. Now, his human form is like that of a crazed hermit living on the fringes of human society. His silver hair is so thin it's like spider silk and grows down to his waist in length. He is no longer fully bipedal, instead hopping around on all fours like some kind of intelligent ape. His polar bear coat, once pristine and fashionable, is now a tattered, filthy mess that hangs about him like rags. <br /> <br /> <br /> Whatever is left of Rutfol's original personality is warped beyond recognition. Where once he hoped humanity could retain most of its intelligence, he now seeks to strip it away entirely. From the privacy of his hermitage, he carries out gruesome experiments on kidnapped humans, turning them into feral and primitive Chimeras. If mankind will not voluntarily abandon technology, he will force them to do so!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T17:01:48-08:00","id":816508,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Abhaya:</b> Scion of Vishnu<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Role:</b> God of Healing<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> For most Scions, achieving divinity is their penultimate goal, surviving this war long enough to be welcomed into the pantheon and earning the worship and praise of mortals for (hopefully) eternity. But for Abhaya, he was born to godhood, a member of the Devas since he first came into existence. Yet despite having access to power and status mortals have been striving for centuries to immitate, he was unsatisfied with his current station. Abhaya believed that in order to properly defend the World and its mortal inhabitants from the Titans, he needed to experience life from their point of view. And so, like so many Devas before him, Abhaya subjected himself to reincarnation, being born as a mortal with latent Scion potential.<br /> <br /> <br /> His mortal avatar was born into a poverty stricken, yet devout family who's spirituality gave them the strength to endure what others might not. In time, he would receive his visitation by Vishnu, who became his patron sponsor during his time as a Scion. Abhaya possessed none of his memories from his time as a God and viewed the world with mortal eyes, even as his Legend grew. Knowing what it was like to have to scrape by to survive, Abhaya devoted his newly awakened powers to helping the needy mortals of the World, becoming famous among the Scion community for his kindness towards others.<br /> <br /> <br /> During their travels, Abhaya came upon the aftermath of an attack by Vritra, the Titan of Droubt. It had greedily consumed the entire water supply within several miles of a village, causing the land to go barren, plants to wither and people weakened by thirst. Abhaya felt the parched land beneath his feet, the once fertile soil now lifeless sand. In full view of the village, Abhaya approached the dried ditch that had once been their source of nourishment, knelt at its base and literally cried them a river. His ichor fueled tears restored life and vigor to all that they touched, causing the land to bloom once more.For this act, Abhaya was granted apotheosis, becoming a God of healing and earning him the eternal scorn of Vritra for restoring water to a land it had drank empty.<br /> <br /> <br /> Abhaya's godly form has perpetual tears running down his cheeks, a permanent reminder of the deed that elevated him back to his original position. He possesses four arms , light skin and dark brown hair which he keeps long and tied into three buns. One on each side of his head, with the third being on top. He dresses in traditional Hindu fashion, often consisting of light fabric and breezy styles. He does not appear to be a warrior, his body more slim and calmly than the muscular, battle hardened Devas engaged in this war.<br /> <br /> <br /> Having lived as one of them, Abhaya now understands the suffering of mortals and the toll this war has on their lives. While the other Devas are left fighting the Titans on the front lines, Abhaya stays behind to clean up the mess. He visits the war torn landscapes and the terrified, injured mortals and eases their suffering as best he can. Which considering he's a God, means he can do quite a lot! His disguises in the mortal World have included political activists, a volunteer clinic worker, and a self suffecient hunting expert. Whatever his disguise is, he is focused on helping people overcome their problems and recover from any damage they might have caused.<br /> <br /> <br /> Abhaya's Scions are likewise generous individuals who can't help but get involved in other people's business. While their intentions are noble at heart, not all of them are good at expressing it, which can lead to them receiving negative attention or being perceived as too nosy for their own good. Yet Abhaya greatly respects those who use their supernatural powers for the good of others and Scions who fulfill this criteria will find themselves blessed with great rewards by Abhaya so long as they keep it up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Associated Powers:</b> Epic Charisma, Epic Perception, Epic Wits, Fertility, Water, Health, Samsura, Guardian, Animal (Fresh Water Fish)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Associated Skills:</b> Empathy, Awareness, Animal Ken, Politics, Medicine, Survival</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-05-2016, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T15:21:54-08:00","id":820603,"title":"","content":"<b>Ganymede:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Scion of Aphrodite</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>AKA:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Pulos</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Role:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> God of Prostitution</span><br /> <br /> <b>Nature:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Libertine</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Born under the name Chase Pulos, the one who would become known as Ganymede was quite the embarrassing child to raise. From an exceedingly young age, he exhibited sexual curiosity long before he was even ready for puberty. This resulted in him getting into trouble on multiple occasions without even knowing why. When puberty finally did hit him, his libido was nearly insatiable, often finding himself grinding on pillows, lamp posts and door frames. It was around this point that Aphrodite provided him a visitation, if only to stop her son from embarrassing the both of them.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Chase's sex drive did not dissipate with his visitation, but it did help him clarify where it originated from. Now that he had some answers, he was ready to direct it to something more constructive than base urges. After doing some research on his divine parent, he discovered Aphrodite was a patron to prostitutes, and so Chase decided to become a pimp! The young Scion rationalized his career choice as bringing in more servants to Aphrodite; the fringe benefits and perks that came with the job were just a bonus.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Over time, Chase Pulos would prove himself to be more than just an exploiter of the sex trade. He took care of his workers and came down hard on those who sought to abuse them. In doing so, he was modestly respected by those under his employ, which afforded him even more benefits that he gleefully enjoyed. Eventually, Chase moved on from simply recruiting whores and onto rescuing them, challenging less reputable pimps and claiming their workers for his own. By the time he became a Demigod, he was viewed as a patron defender of prostitutes.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">As a God, Ganymede's lust is nearly insatiable even among the ranks of the Dodekatheon. He prides himself on having sex no less than three times a day. Yet unless he is in a bad mood, he rarely disrespects his partners; making sure they are comfortable and in good health. He continues to watch over the prostitutes of the world both male and female, as Ganymede is bisexual. Having received his visitation at 21 years old, he rose to minor divinity in just seven years. Despite his status as a lesser God, he appears to be in no hurry to advance himself, likely basking in the accomplishments he has already achieved.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">In his Godly form, Ganymede mockingly takes the shape of one of the wealthiest pimps you will ever see. He wears thick, animal fur coats with excessive jewelery encrusted with precious gemstones that sparkle in the light. A pair of tinted sunglasses obscures his eyes from sight and he travels with at least two nymphs at his side which are of random species. The golden, diamond headed cane he carries is a Relic forged by Hephaestus which allows him to channel the Earth purview and functions as a Maquahuitl in combat. The coat he wears allows him to channel the Animal and Health purviews and adds +1L, +2B to the Heavy Clothing armor. Finally, he wields a gold plated hand gun which adds +2 Accuracy and +3L to the Glock template.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Ganymede may be a lech, but he respects those who work for him and he expects his children to do the same with their own charges. Scions of Ganymede are peculiar as they exhibit many deviant behaviors, yet follow some code of personal honor designed to keep them from going out of control. Scions who break this code may find themselves receiving a swift visit from the back of their father's ring adorned hand!</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Associated Powers:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Epic Appearance, Epic Charisma, Epic Stamina, Epic Perception, Arete, Earth, Health, Animal </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Animal Ken, Empathy, Presence, Melee, Marksmanship, Integrity</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-31-2016, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}